  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:linear-encoder",
  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "A Linear Encoder is a position sensing device that measures linear (translational) displacement along a single axis by converting physical motion into an electrical signal \u2014 typically a series of digital pulses or an analogue waveform \u2014 that a controller can interpret as position, velocity, or acceleration data. Linear encoders may be optical (using a diffraction grating or glass scale), magnetic (using a magnetised tape), or capacitive, with resolution ranging from micrometres to nanometres in precision metrology applications. They are essential feedback elements in CNC machine tools, semiconductor lithography stages, and high-precision robotic manipulators where closed-loop positional accuracy is required.",
